From 4e19cf21f6b87f57d34e5ba741eda091b03a8e2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:58:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: a boot self-test of every texture path (fixing or
 dropping what isn't exact), game code at -O2 without per-call instrumentation

t13 put the texture cache's atlas in memory of our own and checked it every frame. The checks
were clean for a whole run (0 stale slots, 0 descriptors pointed back), yet every cached texel
was still drawn from 6 to its left: the slots held the right texels where the descriptor
pointed, and the GPU read them shifted. The renderer now measures this at boot instead of
guessing.

The self-test (THPS_GL_SELFTEST=0 skips it) uploads a 16-bit test page whose every texel's colour
spells its u and row. It draws it through every way a draw reads a texture, as the game draws:
the emulated lookup on the store's texture, the cache at slots in the atlas's corners and middle,
a blit (copy program, pool texture) and a movie picture (present program, pool texture). It reads
each row back from the base target, with a flat white pixel after each as the read-back's own
reference, and logs what the GPU returned ("[gl] self-test: ..." lines). Anything not exact is
fixed or dropped before the game draws:
- The cache tries the other atlas shape (2048x4096, the same 128 slots).
- If both shapes are off, it undoes the shift they share, first in the descriptor's address,
  then in the shader (u_atlasFix).
- If none of that is exact, the cache turns off.
- The store's own copies give way to vitaGL's texture.
- The blit and movie-picture pools give way to vitaGL's copies.
The atlas's shape and correction are now shader uniforms (u_atlasCols, u_atlasScale,
u_atlasFix) instead of constants.

Speed: in t13's slow scenes a level frame was ~35 ms of CPU (swap under 7 ms). The game code is
now built at -O2 (THPS_VITA_OPT=1 gives -O1 again), without identical-code folding (function
pointers the game compares stay distinct) or the vectoriser. -finstrument-functions, two calls
more on every game call for the stall sampler, is only built with THPS_VITA_INSTRUMENT=1; without
it the profile has no [stall-fn] or [stall-top] lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
